            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "What kind of federal policies will bring US home prices down?",
            "description": "<p>As mortgage rates tick lower in the first week of 2026, President Trump has called for Fannie Mae (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/FNMA\">FNMA</a>) and Freddie Mac (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/FMCC\">FMCC</a>) to acquire more mortgage bonds.</p>\n<p>Redfin chief economist Daryl Fairweather discusses what kinds of federal policies could effectively lower US home prices.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination-overtime/\">Market Domination Overtime</a>.</p>",
